ished, consumed, destroyed: people Num 14:33 ( J ), v Num 14:35 ; Num 17:28 ( P ; || מות ). Num 32:13 ( J ), Josh 8:24 ; Josh 10:20 ( J E ), Deut 2:14 ; Deut 2:15 ; Deut 2:16 ; Josh 5:6 ( D ), 1Kgs 14:10 ; 2Kgs 7:13 ; Isa 16:4 ; Jer 14:15 ; Jer 24:10 ; Jer 27:8 ; Jer 36:23 ; Jer 44:12 (twice in verse); Jer 44:18 ; Jer 44:27 ; Ps 9:7 (but read דַּמּוּ ), Ps 104:35 . 6. be complete, sound, unimpaired , ethically, Ps 19:14 (|| נִקָּה ; late). 7. twice, very strangely, si vera 1., transitive: Ps 64:7 תמנו we have completed (read probably הֲתִמֹּנוּ ); Jer 27:8 עַדתֻּֿמֹּי אֹתָם בְּיָדוֺ (read with Gr תִּתִּי ). Hiph`il Perfect 1 singular הֲתִמֹּ֫תִי Ezek 22:15 3 masculine plural הֵחַמּ֫וּ 2Sam 20:18 Imperfect יַתֵּם 2Kgs 22:4 2 masculine singular תַּתֵּם Job 22:3 ( Ges «GKC:67y»§ 67y ); Infinitive absolute הָחֵם Ezek 24:10 construct, id. , Dan 8:23 + Dan 9:24 Qr (see Dr .); suffix הֲִתמְךְ ( Ges «GKC:67v»§ 67v ) Isa 33:1 — 1. finish, complete, perfect , a matter 2Sam 20:18 (but Qal , come to an end , with ה interrogative, We Dr and others); flesh in cooking Ezek 24:10 . 2. finish, cease doing a thing, followed by participle ( Ges «GKC:120b»§ 120b ), שׁוֺדֵד Isa 33:1 . 3. complete, sum up , with accusative money 2Kgs 22:4 (other conjectures Klo Gr Gi ); transgressions Dan 8:23 sin Dan 9:24 ( Qr ; Kt חתם ). 4. destroy uncleanness, with מן from , Ezek 22:15 . 5. causative (of Qal 6 ): accusative דרכיך Job 22:3 make sound thy ways. Hithpa`el Imperfect 2 masculine singular תִּתַּמָּם 2Sam 22:26 , with עִם deal in integrity with = Ps 18:26 (late, see Qal 6 ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9189')\">BDB9189</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8552')\">H8552</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9188')\">BDB9188</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9190')\">BDB9190</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>תָּמַם</bdbheb>], <bdbheb>תַּם</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be complete, finished</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder5